PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_13humpy_cytoolz_9itertoolz_40pluck, "pluck(ind, seqs, default=\047__no__default__\047)\n\nPlucks an element or several elements from each item in a sequence.\n\n``pluck`` maps ``itertoolz.get`` over a sequence and returns one or more\nelements of each item in the sequence.\n\nThis is equivalent to running `map(curried.get(ind), seqs)`\n\n``ind`` can be either a single string/index or a list of strings/indices.\n``seqs`` should be sequence containing sequences or dicts.\n\ne.g.\n\n>>> data = [{\047id\047: 1, \047name\047: \047Cheese\047}, {\047id\047: 2, \047name\047: \047Pies\047}]\n>>> list(pluck(\047name\047, data))\n[\047Cheese\047, \047Pies\047]\n>>> list(pluck([0, 1], [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 7]]))\n[(1, 2), (4, 5)]\n\nSee Also\n--------\n        get\n        map");
